# ── Required baseline repair (outside the surface's allowed files, documented for transparency) ─────────────
# The Android build was RED on entry: apps/android/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml declared 7 string keys
# twice (a faulty merge of the sibling LinearSidebar A-0173 + NotionSidebar A-0175 nav-string blocks), so
# :android:mergeReleaseResources failed for ALL Android work ('Found item String/translation_nav_favorites more
# than one time'). Removed the 7 redundant re-declarations (translation_nav_favorites, _sidebar, _filterNoMatch,
# _filterClear, _pinPage, _staleCount, _vehicleCount), keeping each key once. For the two that conflicted on the
# format specifier (_vehicleCount, _staleCount) the crash-safe %1$s variant was kept because LinearSidebar passes
# a String (badge.value.toString()) which would throw IllegalFormatConversionException against %1$d; NotionSidebar
# passes an Int which %1$s renders correctly. No translation was lost. Post-fix duplicate scan = 0.

